---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import {
    IconBuildingCommunity,
    IconChevronDown,
    IconJewishStar,
    IconLanguage,
    IconMenorah,
    IconMoodKid,
    IconScale,
    IconSchool,
    IconScript,
    IconShirt,
    IconUsers,
} from '@tabler/icons-astro';
---

<PageLayout title="FAQ - Ohr HaTorah" pageTitle="Frequently Asked Questions">
    <p class="faq-intro">Welcome to Messianic Judaism! Here are answers to common questions for newcomers.</p>

    <div class="faq-container">
        <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
                <IconJewishStar class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>What is Messianic Judaism?</span>
                <IconChevronDown class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true" />
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer" hidden>
                <p>Messianic Judaism is a movement of Jewish people who believe that Yeshua (Jesus) is the promised Messiah of Israel, while maintaining Jewish identity, traditions, and observance of Torah.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
                <IconUsers class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>Do I need to be Jewish to attend?</span>
                <IconChevronDown class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true" />
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer" hidden>
                <p>Absolutely not! We welcome all people - Jewish, non-Jewish, and interfaith families. Everyone is invited to learn and grow in understanding of our Jewish Messiah.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
                <IconBuildingCommunity class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>What should I expect during a service?</span>
                <IconChevronDown class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true" />
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer" hidden>
                <p>Our services include contemporary Messianic music, traditional Hebrew prayers, Torah reading, and teaching. Services are conducted in both Hebrew and English with explanations provided.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
                <IconMenorah class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>Do you follow Jewish holidays and traditions?</span>
                <IconChevronDown class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true" />
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer" hidden>
                <p>Yes! We observe Shabbat, biblical holidays like Passover and Yom Kippur, and maintain Jewish traditions while recognizing Yeshua as our Messiah.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
                <IconLanguage class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>Is Hebrew required?</span>
                <IconChevronDown class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true" />
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer" hidden>
                <p>Not at all. We use Hebrew in prayers and readings, but everything is explained in English. Contact us about current Hebrew learning opportunities.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
                <IconScript class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>What is the Torah?</span>
                <IconChevronDown class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true" />
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer" hidden>
                <p>The Torah is the first five books of the Bible (Genesis through Deuteronomy), containing God's instructions for living. We believe Torah remains relevant for believers today.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
                <IconScale class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>How is Messianic Judaism different from Christianity?</span>
                <IconChevronDown class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true" />
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer" hidden>
                <p>While we believe in Yeshua as Messiah, we maintain Jewish practices, celebrate biblical feasts, and emphasize the Jewish context of faith rather than adopting Gentile Christian traditions.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
                <IconShirt class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>What should I wear to services?</span>
                <IconChevronDown class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true" />
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer" hidden>
                <p>Come as you are! We welcome casual to semi-formal attire. Men may wear a kippah (yarmulke) if desired, but it's not required for visitors.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
                <IconMoodKid class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>Can children attend?</span>
                <IconChevronDown class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true" />
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer" hidden>
                <p>Yes. Families with children are very welcome. A Shabbat School for youth is in development as our congregation grows.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
                <IconSchool class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>How can I learn more?</span>
                <IconChevronDown class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true" />
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer" hidden>
                <p>Visit us for Shabbat services, speak with Rabbi Charles, explore the resources on this site, or contact us with a specific question.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</PageLayout>

<script>
    // FAQ Accordion functionality
    const faqItems = document.querySelectorAll('.faq-item');
    faqItems.forEach(item => {
        const question = item.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.faq-question');
        const answer = item.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.faq-answer');
        if (question && answer) {
            question.addEventListener('click', () => {
                const expanding = question.getAttribute('aria-expanded') !== 'true';
                // Close other open items
                faqItems.forEach(otherItem => {
                    if (otherItem !== item && otherItem.classList.contains('active')) {
                        otherItem.classList.remove('active');
                        otherItem.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.faq-question')?.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
                        const otherAnswer = otherItem.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.faq-answer');
                        if (otherAnswer) otherAnswer.hidden = true;
                    }
                });
                // Toggle current item
                item.classList.toggle('active', expanding);
                question.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(expanding));
                answer.hidden = !expanding;
            });
        }
    });
</script>

<style>
    .faq-intro {
        text-align: center;
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        margin-bottom: 30px;
    }

    .faq-container {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 15px;
    }

    .faq-item {
        border: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
        border-radius: 8px;
        overflow: hidden;
        transition: all 0.3s ease;
    }

    .faq-item:hover {
        border-color: var(--primary-blue);
    }

    .faq-question {
        display: flex;
        width: 100%;
        align-items: center;
        border: 0;
        text-align: left;
        padding: 20px;
        cursor: pointer;
        background: var(--gray-100);
        transition: background 0.3s ease;
    }

    .faq-question:hover {
        background: var(--gray-200);
    }

    .faq-icon {
        color: var(--primary-blue);
        font-size: 1.2rem;
        margin-right: 15px;
        min-width: 25px;
        text-align: center;
    }

    .faq-question span {
        font-weight: 600;
        color: var(--text-primary);
        flex: 1;
    }

    .faq-chevron {
        width: 20px;
        height: 20px;
        flex: 0 0 auto;
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        transition: transform 0.3s ease;
    }

    .faq-item.active .faq-chevron {
        transform: rotate(180deg);
    }

    .faq-answer {
        max-height: 0;
        overflow: hidden;
        transition: max-height 0.3s ease;
    }

    .faq-item.active .faq-answer {
        max-height: 500px;
    }

    .faq-answer p {
        padding: 20px;
        margin: 0;
        background: white;
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        line-height: 1.6;
    }

    @media (max-width: 767px) {
        .faq-question {
            align-items: flex-start;
            padding: 16px;
        }

        .faq-answer p {
            padding: 16px;
        }
    }
</style>
